.TH SSH2FACTOTUM 8
.SH NAME
ssh2factotum \- convert an OpenSSH ed25519 key to a factotum key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B auth/ssh2factotum
[
.I file
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Ssh2factotum
reads an OpenSSH private key, as
.B ssh-keygen
.B -t
.B ed25519
writes it, from
.I file
or from its standard input, and prints it as a key for
.IR factotum (4):
.IP
.EX
key proto=ed25519 pk=\fIpublic\fP comment=\fIcomment\fP !sk=\fIsecret\fP
.EE
.PP
.I Public
is the key's public half and
.I secret
its 32-byte seed, each in hexadecimal.
.I Comment
is the key's comment, quoted as
.IR quote (2)
quotes; a key with no comment has no
.B comment=
attribute.
The secret is in a
.B !
attribute, so
.I factotum
does not show it.
.PP
The key must be in the
.B openssh-key-v1
format, between the lines
.B "-----BEGIN OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY-----"
and
.BR "-----END OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY-----" ,
hold one key, and have no passphrase.
.SH EXAMPLES
Give
.I factotum
the key that
.B ssh
uses, for
.B auth/ssh-agent
to sign with:
.IP
.EX
auth/ssh2factotum $home/lib/ssh/id_ed25519 >/mnt/factotum/ctl
.EE
.PP
Remove the passphrase from a copy of a key that has one first:
.IP
.EX
cp id_ed25519 /tmp/k
ssh-keygen -p -N '' -f /tmp/k
auth/ssh2factotum /tmp/k >/mnt/factotum/ctl
rm /tmp/k
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/cmd/auth/ssh2factotum.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR factotum (4),
.IR auth (8)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.I Ssh2factotum
prints nothing on its standard output when it fails.
It fails when the input has no
.B OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY
lines or is not an
.B openssh-key-v1
key.
It fails when the key has a passphrase, when the file holds more than one key, and when the check
bytes differ.
It fails when the key's type is not
.BR ssh-ed25519 ,
when a half of the key has the wrong length, and when the secret half's public half is not the key's.
.SH BUGS
It converts only ed25519 keys.
